# Opcode 0x40 Handler - Zoom Value Decoding

The opcode 0x40 handler processes video drawing with conditional zoom parameter handling. Here's the relevant section:

## Zoom Case Handling

```c
uint16_t zoom = _scriptPtr.fetchByte();

if (!(opcode & 2))  // 0000 0010 is set
{
    if (!(opcode & 1)) // 0000 0001 is set
    {
        --_scriptPtr.pc;
        zoom = 0x40;
    } 
    else 
    {
        zoom = vmVariables[zoom];
    }
} 
else 
{
    if (opcode & 1) { // 0000 0001 is set
        res->_useSegVideo2 = true;
        --_scriptPtr.pc;
        zoom = 0x40;
    }
}
```

## Zoom Decoding Summary

The zoom parameter is decoded using opcode bits 1-2:

- **Bits [2:1] = 00**: Default zoom (0x40); script pointer decremented
- **Bits [2:1] = 01**: Zoom loaded from variable indexed by fetched byte
- **Bits [2:1] = 10**: Fetched byte used as zoom value
- **Bits [2:1] = 11**: Default zoom (0x40) with segment flag set; script pointer decremented

The script pointer adjustment (`--_scriptPtr.pc`) occurs when the zoom byte is fetched but not consumed as an actual zoom value.

